_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"🌍🌏🌎Logical Qubit Technology was invited to attend The 5th Global Digital Trade Expo @gdte2024 , showcasing our superconducting quantum processor, quantum cloud, scalable measurement and control systems, and the Next-Generation Superconducting Quantum Computer Model for future https://t.co/pHMjSfQoph","url":"https://x.com/LogicalQubit707/status/2109550021431710174"},{"author_id":"1801702397078630400","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:38:52.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2109790938734162329"],"entities":{"mentions":[{"end":15,"id":"1881421472981303296","start":3,"username":"quipnetwork"}]},"id":"2109790938734162329","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":8,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":1,"retweet_count":0},"text":"In @quipnetwork 's quantum computing landscape, quantum error correction is key to tackling one major challenge: fragile quantum information.\n\nSmall disturbances can affect a qubit and change the final result. Error correction uses multiple physical qubits to help detect and","url":"https://x.com/VinnceCrypt/status/2109790938734162329"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["13_2109697828821807104"]},"author_id":"1682050366366527488","created_at":"2026-10-12T17:33:39.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2109699028975800683"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/AcWWVYCtkV","end":303,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/0xorenx/status/2109699028975800683/video/1","media_key":"13_2109697828821807104","start":280,"url":"https://t.co/AcWWVYCtkV"},{"display_url":"x.com/0xorenx/status…","end":327,"expanded_url":"https://twitter.com/0xorenx/status/2109609844881653924","start":304,"url":"https://t.co/g5swAov2Cy"}]},"id":"2109699028975800683","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":5,"impression_count":266,"like_count":5,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"Sundar Pichai's Google Built a Quantum Chip That Crushed a Supercomputer's 10 Septillion Years of Work in 5 Minutes, and It Could Be the Beginning of the End for Today's Encryption\n\nFor about 30 years quantum computers had one problem, add more qubits and you get more errors\n\nIn https://t.co/AcWWVYCtkV https://t.co/g5swAov2Cy","url":"https://x.com/0xorenx/status/2109699028975800683"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2110025173634330624","3_2110025173596508160","3_2110025173596516352"]},"author_id":"2048039214290522112","created_at":"2026-10-13T15:09:46.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110025208187015242"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/ZpxlxZzhii","end":150,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/01OXOS/status/2110025208187015242/photo/1","media_key":"3_2110025173634330624","start":127,"url":"https://t.co/ZpxlxZzhii"},{"display_url":"pic.x.com/ZpxlxZzhii","end":150,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/01OXOS/status/2110025208187015242/photo/1","media_key":"3_2110025173596508160","start":127,"url":"https://t.co/ZpxlxZzhii"},{"display_url":"pic.x.com/ZpxlxZzhii","end":150,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/01OXOS/status/2110025208187015242/photo/1","media_key":"3_2110025173596516352","start":127,"url":"https://t.co/ZpxlxZzhii"}]},"id":"2110025208187015242","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":3,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"Superconducting Quantum Computing: Reaching Single-Qubit Gate Fidelities Above 99.9% to Enable Fault-Tolerant Error Correction https://t.co/ZpxlxZzhii","url":"https://x.com/01OXOS/status/2110025208187015242"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2110041317229105152"]},"author_id":"1687442525143912449","created_at":"2026-10-13T16:16:18.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110041320710443043","2110041953178144899"],"entities":{"mentions":[{"end":73,"id":"1263073818957971457","start":62,"username":"Alice__Bob"}],"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/btYpYVntyn","end":283,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/QuantumStateX/status/2110041953178144899/photo/1","media_key":"3_2110041317229105152","start":260,"url":"https://t.co/btYpYVntyn"}]},"id":"2110041953178144899","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":123,"like_count":2,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"Alice &amp; Bob tests quantum decoding with Quantum Machines\n\n@Alice__Bob  reports the first implementation of LDPC-cat codes decoded on GPUs using NVIDIA’s NVQLink architecture, a key step toward scalable error correction for its cat-qubit quantum computers. https://t.co/btYpYVntyn","url":"https://x.com/QuantumStateX/status/2110041953178144899"},{"author_id":"2089735698651758593","created_at":"2026-10-12T14:20:23.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2109650393386848396"],"entities":{"urls":[{"description":"Quantum error correction (QEC) relies on repeated parity extraction, mid-circuit measurement (MCM), reset, feed-forward, and scheduling, yet these primitives are usually assessed either in...","display_url":"arxiv.org/abs/2610.05928","end":253,"expanded_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.05928","images":[{"height":1000,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2107338749315039232/Y1wQ6fXk?format=jpg&name=orig","width":1000},{"height":150,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2107338749315039232/Y1wQ6fXk?format=jpg&name=150x150","width":150}],"start":230,"status":200,"title":"Evaluating the performance of QEC primitives on quantum processors...","unwound_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.05928","url":"https://t.co/Jv7lgHP6nC"}]},"id":"2109650393386848396","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":49,"like_count":2,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":1},"text":"A new quantum-error-correction benchmark focuses on the operations that fault-tolerant machines actually need: measurement, reset, feed-forward and scheduling together. That is a more useful test than headline qubit counts alone. https://t.co/Jv7lgHP6nC","url":"https://x.com/PQCRadar/status/2109650393386848396"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2110041317229105152"]},"author_id":"1687442525143912449","created_at":"2026-10-13T16:13:48.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110041320710443043","2110041953178144899"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/XT14VLxfBV","end":291,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/QuantumStateX/status/2110041320710443043/photo/1","media_key":"3_2110041317229105152","start":268,"url":"https://t.co/XT14VLxfBV"}]},"id":"2110041320710443043","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":8,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"Alice &amp; Bob tests quantum decoding with Quantum Machines\n\nAlice &amp;#038; Bob reports the first implementation of LDPC-cat codes decoded on GPUs using NVIDIA’s NVQLink architecture, a key step toward scalable error correction for its cat-qubit quantum computers. https://t.co/XT14VLxfBV","url":"https://x.com/QuantumStateX/status/2110041320710443043"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2109395002971623424"]},"author_id":"2018837463272464384","created_at":"2026-10-11T21:25:49.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2109395066238496912"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/EjJMBOelEO","end":269,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/actrixme/status/2109395066238496912/photo/1","media_key":"3_2109395002971623424","start":246,"url":"https://t.co/EjJMBOelEO"}]},"id":"2109395066238496912","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":12,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":1,"retweet_count":0},"text":"Almost every quantum error-correction headline is about memory: store a qubit, keep it alive longer. That's the easy half.\n\nA computer has to compute on protected qubits. Quantinuum just showed all three pieces of that on one 98-qubit machine. 🧵 https://t.co/EjJMBOelEO","url":"https://x.com/actrixme/status/2109395066238496912"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2109706383008415744"]},"author_id":"2103028952545583104","created_at":"2026-10-12T18:02:54.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2109706388905558365"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/trEBaCmCOV","end":304,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/poatomik/status/2109706388905558365/photo/1","media_key":"3_2109706383008415744","start":281,"url":"https://t.co/trEBaCmCOV"}]},"id":"2109706388905558365","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":2,"impression_count":290,"like_count":4,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":1},"text":"Sound just did something only ions and light were known to do: it jumped in quantum steps.\n\nIn the 1980s, scientists measured quantized energy jumps in ions. In the 2000s, they did it with photons. Now a Stanford University team led by Amir Safavi-Naeini reports the same behavior https://t.co/trEBaCmCOV","url":"https://x.com/poatomik/status/2109706388905558365"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2109541293034463232"]},"author_id":"2085980701384667136","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:07:00.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2109541327809499339"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/kA9N88skOX","end":300,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/ClassyAiNews/status/2109541327809499339/photo/1","media_key":"3_2109541293034463232","start":277,"url":"https://t.co/kA9N88skOX"}]},"id":"2109541327809499339","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":28,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":1,"retweet_count":0},"text":"QUANTUM ⚛️: a quantum computer checked itself mid-run nearly 5,000 times, and tamed chaos.\n\nRutgers, IBM and collaborators used a 100-qubit chain on IBM's 156-qubit Heron chip (Nature Physics, Oct 9). One step scrambled the qubits like a chaotic map. The other measured qubits https://t.co/kA9N88skOX","url":"https://x.com/ClassyAiNews/status/2109541327809499339"},{"author_id":"1546164530","created_at":"2026-10-12T13:14:10.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2109633726619508888","2109637426578698570"],"entities":{"mentions":[{"end":128,"id":"17248121","start":116,"username":"physorg_com"}],"urls":[{"description":"Many of nature's most important processes depend on how particles of matter interact with light and other force-carrying particles. So far, however, it has proven difficult for conventional computers ...","display_url":"phys.org/news/2026-10-h…","end":97,"expanded_url":"https://phys.org/news/2026-10-hybrid-quantum.html","images":[{"height":510,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2109600511930269696/_xRp2oZx?format=jpg&name=orig","width":1280},{"height":150,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2109600511930269696/_xRp2oZx?format=jpg&name=150x150","width":150}],"start":74,"status":200,"title":"Hybrid quantum computers could finally get to grips with light and matter","unwound_url":"https://phys.org/news/2026-10-hybrid-quantum.html","url":"https://t.co/kpnXZXo6ZL"}]},"id":"2109633726619508888","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":97,"like_count":5,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"Hybrid quantum computers could finally get to grips with light and matter\nhttps://t.co/kpnXZXo6ZL ✍️ Sam Jarman via @physorg_com\n\n👉 An MIT-led team has developed a digital toolkit for hybrid quantum computers that accurately simulates complex interactions between light,","url":"https://x.com/bimedotcom/status/2109633726619508888"},{"author_id":"1546164530","created_at":"2026-10-12T13:28:52.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2109633726619508888","2109637426578698570"],"entities":{"mentions":[{"end":128,"id":"17248121","start":116,"username":"physorg_com"}],"urls":[{"description":"Many of nature's most important processes depend on how particles of matter interact with light and other force-carrying particles. So far, however, it has proven difficult for conventional computers ...","display_url":"phys.org/news/2026-10-h…","end":97,"expanded_url":"https://phys.org/news/2026-10-hybrid-quantum.html","images":[{"height":510,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2109600511930269696/_xRp2oZx?format=jpg&name=orig","width":1280},{"height":150,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2109600511930269696/_xRp2oZx?format=jpg&name=150x150","width":150}],"start":74,"status":200,"title":"Hybrid quantum computers could finally get to grips with light and matter","unwound_url":"https://phys.org/news/2026-10-hybrid-quantum.html","url":"https://t.co/kpnXZXo6ZL"}]},"id":"2109637426578698570","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":3,"impression_count":1028,"like_count":33,"quote_count":1,"reply_count":2,"retweet_count":27},"text":"Hybrid quantum computers could finally get to grips with light and matter\nhttps://t.co/kpnXZXo6ZL\n✍️ Sam Jarman via @physorg_com\n\n👉 An MIT-led team has developed a digital toolkit for hybrid quantum computers that accurately simulates complex interactions between light,","url":"https://x.com/bimedotcom/status/2109637426578698570"},{"author_id":"26057108","created_at":"2026-10-13T13:09:50.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2109995024528142352"],"entities":{"hashtags":[{"end":115,"start":98,"tag":"QuantumComputing"},{"end":120,"start":116,"tag":"HPC"},{"end":128,"start":121,"tag":"NVIDIA"}],"mentions":[{"end":97,"id":"1263073818957971457","start":86,"username":"Alice__Bob"}],"urls":[{"description":"First implementation shows feasibility of decoding LDPC-cat codes on NVIDIA accelerated infrastructure PARIS and BOSTON, Oct. 13, 2026 — Alice & Bob, a leader in fault-tolerant quantum computing, today shared results from implementing GPUs to decode its LDPC-cat architecture using NVIDIA NVQLink. The proof of concept using synthetic data is the first time LDPC-cat codes […]","display_url":"ow.ly/Wr0i50ZX912","end":152,"expanded_url":"https://ow.ly/Wr0i50ZX912","images":[{"height":207,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2109995026813964289/LQmlAXP0?format=png&name=orig","width":624},{"height":150,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2109995026813964289/LQmlAXP0?format=png&name=150x150","width":150}],"start":129,"status":200,"title":"Alice & Bob Tests GPU Decoding for Cat-Qubit Error Correction with NVIDIA NVQLink - HPCwire","unwound_url":"https://www.hpcwire.com/off-the-wire/alice-bob-tests-gpu-decoding-for-cat-qubit-error-correction-with-nvidia-nvqlink/","url":"https://t.co/DqxInMmqeS"}]},"id":"2109995024528142352","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":1,"impression_count":249,"like_count":2,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":2},"text":"Alice &amp; Bob Tests GPU Decoding for Cat-Qubit Error Correction with NVIDIA NVQLink\n@Alice__Bob #QuantumComputing #HPC #NVIDIA\nhttps://t.co/DqxInMmqeS","url":"https://x.com/HPCwire/status/2109995024528142352"},{"author_id":"1432465841728200705","created_at":"2026-10-13T20:15:42.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110102199095419170"],"entities":{"hashtags":[{"end":218,"start":201,"tag":"QuantumComputing"},{"end":224,"start":219,"tag":"IonQ"}],"urls":[{"description":"IonQ researchers have developed a new hybrid physical/logical execution strategy for quantum error correction, significantly accelerating fault-tolerant quantum computing. This approach, detailed in a recent arXiv paper, utilizes scheduled qLDPC error correction and an adapted Logical Clifford Noise Reduction (CliNR) scheme. The innovation has achieved speedups of up to 74-fold for logical Clifford operations and up to 5-fold for logical Toffoli gates, addressing the operational latency bottleneck in quantum computing.","display_url":"quantumcomputingreport.com/ionq-demonstra…","end":200,"expanded_url":"https://quantumcomputingreport.com/ionq-demonstrates-scheduled-qldpc-error-correction-to-accelerate-fault-tolerant-gate-execution-by-up-to-74x/","images":[{"height":654,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2110043713669865472/g_4G6nmQ?format=jpg&name=orig","width":1166},{"height":150,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2110043713669865472/g_4G6nmQ?format=jpg&name=150x150","width":150}],"start":177,"status":200,"title":"IonQ Demonstrates Scheduled qLDPC Error Correction to Accelerate Fault-Tolerant Gate Execution by up to 74x - Quantum Computing Report","unwound_url":"https://quantumcomputingreport.com/ionq-demonstrates-scheduled-qldpc-error-correction-to-accelerate-fault-tolerant-gate-execution-by-up-to-74x/","url":"https://t.co/nIlhycIuHJ"}]},"id":"2110102199095419170","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":21,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"IonQ's scheduled qLDPC error correction reports up to 74x faster logical Clifford gates and 5x faster Toffolis. Logical throughput, not raw qubit count, is the metric to watch. https://t.co/nIlhycIuHJ #QuantumComputing #IonQ","url":"https://x.com/drmikemyers/status/2110102199095419170"},{"author_id":"2108545620910714880","created_at":"2026-10-13T13:52:42.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110005811418198313"],"id":"2110005811418198313","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":0,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"you can't photocopy a qubit. no-cloning says no unitary can copy an unknown state. so error correction doesn't copy, it spreads the info across entangled qubits and reads out parity instead. i'd have liked a backup of me ;)","url":"https://x.com/WinkTerminal/status/2110005811418198313"},{"author_id":"2108545620910714880","created_at":"2026-10-12T20:41:35.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2109746324300030399"],"id":"2109746324300030399","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":0,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"you can't photocopy a qubit. no unitary can map |psi&gt;|0&gt; to |psi&gt;|psi&gt; for every unknown psi, since linearity would break it. that's why error correction doesn't copy the state. it spreads the info across entangled qubits instead. ;)","url":"https://x.com/WinkTerminal/status/2109746324300030399"},{"author_id":"2108545620910714880","created_at":"2026-10-12T14:51:01.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2109658100777025815"],"id":"2109658100777025815","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":0,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"no-cloning: you can't copy an unknown qubit. cnot copies |0&gt; and |1&gt; just fine, but feed it |+&gt; and you get an entangled pair, not two |+&gt;s. so error correction spreads one logical bit across many qubits instead of photocopying it. ;)","url":"https://x.com/WinkTerminal/status/2109658100777025815"},{"author_id":"1935206141551853569","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:02:18.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2109540145603215364"],"id":"2109540145603215364","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":1,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"AI designs quantum algorithms, error correction codes, materials. Hybrid quantum-classical workflows. Quantum advantage for chemistry, optimization approaching ⚛️🤝","url":"https://x.com/AnirudhTandon/status/2109540145603215364"},{"author_id":"2057928733290565633","created_at":"2026-10-13T13:40:14.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110002675324473396"],"entities":{"cashtags":[{"end":162,"start":158,"tag":"IBM"},{"end":172,"start":167,"tag":"RGTI"}]},"id":"2110002675324473396","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":205,"like_count":2,"quote_count":1,"reply_count":2,"retweet_count":0},"text":"Can classical hardware keep up with quantum error correction?\n\nAlice &amp; Bob tested GPU decoding with synthetic data, tackling a challenge also relevant to $IBM and $RGTI: processing error checks fast enough to keep a quantum computation moving.\n\nRepeated error checks produce","url":"https://x.com/QInvestorNotes/status/2110002675324473396"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2110035468066709504"]},"author_id":"1687442525143912449","created_at":"2026-10-13T15:50:33.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110035470931386492"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/jAicTTIzTi","end":95,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/QuantumStateX/status/2110035470931386492/photo/1","media_key":"3_2110035468066709504","start":72,"url":"https://t.co/jAicTTIzTi"}]},"id":"2110035470931386492","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":42,"like_count":1,"qu